PR 5 additionally reproduces, from the Deceptive Grounding benchmark (same
commit as above, benchmark_judge.py), licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

  - the text of _JUDGE_SYSTEM_PROMPT, verbatim;
  - the single-condition judge prompt built by _build_judge_prompt, verbatim
    (as a template filled with the item's fields);
  - the logic of _validate_judgment and _parse_judgment, re-implemented.

They are in src/binding_gate/scorers/llm_judge.py (the secondary LLM-judge
scorer). The benchmark's code was read, never imported or executed.

The faithfulness_checker arm (src/binding_gate/arms/faithfulness_checker.py)
calls MiniCheck (https://github.com/Liyan06/MiniCheck, commit
b58b9fa69acbd1015ec970fa65dd752413a053d2, Apache License, Version 2.0) and the
model weights lytang/MiniCheck-Flan-T5-Large (revision
96eafd01cee2d16cf81aaa2fb226b14f422a37b3, MIT License, per its model card)
when the optional "faithfulness" extra is installed. Neither the package nor
the weights are included in this repository.

